# multi_kb.jsonl — AP-A5 / AP-A4 evaluation set
#
# Two purposes:
#  1. AP-A4 sub-KB router: per question, did the router pick the right
#     KB(s)? Top-1 hit-rate target ≥ 0.85.
#  2. Phase C cross-KB retrieval (later): does the search actually
#     surface chunks from the expected KBs?
#
# Schema (extends eval/golden/example.jsonl):
#  - kb_id            primary KB the question runs against
#  - expected_kb_ids  AP-A4 ground truth. Empty (default) = single-KB,
#                     router must pick kb_id. Multi-element = router
#                     should pick at least one element in top-1, and
#                     ideally fan out to all.
#  - must_cite_file_ids   files the retrieval pipeline must surface
#  - notes            human-readable hint; ignored by the runner
#
# Authoring guidance:
#  - 30 single-KB rows: pure router-ambiguity tests. Each question
#    should be answerable from one KB only; the trick is whether the
#    router can tell from the question text alone. Pick questions where
#    surface terms could match other KBs but only one actually
#    contains the answer. Examples in this file: q-skb-001..005.
#  - 20 cross-KB rows: questions whose answer requires evidence from
#    multiple KBs. Example pattern: cross-references between policy
#    documents and project profiles. Examples in this file:
#    q-mkb-001..005.
#  - Use plausible-but-fake UUIDs for `kb_id` and file ids until you
#    paste real ones in. The 00000000-XXXX placeholders below are
#    deliberately invalid for production.
#
# REPLACE-BEFORE-RUN markers (search for "TODO-A5"):
#  - Every kb_id and file_id below is a placeholder.
#  - Replace with real UUIDs from your KBs admin panel before running
#    the AP-A4 evaluator.
#
# To extend the set: append new lines, do NOT rewrite existing ones —
# snapshot diffs key on the stable `id` field.
#
# ---- Single-KB router-ambiguity rows (AP-A4: top-1 hit-rate) ----
